    <string name="setup_restricted_help_title">Did Android say it\'s a restricted setting?</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_help_text">Android blocks this for apps installed from a file. Now that you\'ve seen that message, you can unblock it:\n\n1. Tap Open App info.\n2. Tap ⋮ at the top right, then Allow restricted settings, and confirm.\n3. Come back here and tap Allow again.\n\nYou only need to do this once: it unblocks the other permissions too.</string>
    <string name="setup_not_now">Not now</string>
    <string name="setup_all_set">You\'re all set</string>
    <string name="setup_almost_set">Almost there</string>
    <string name="setup_all_set_text">Everything Wellmute needs is allowed.</string>
    <string name="setup_missing_text">Some features won\'t work until you allow what\'s missing. You can also do it later in Settings → Permissions.</string>
    <string name="setup_open_wellmute">Open Wellmute</string>
    <string name="setup_allow">Allow</string>
    <string name="setup_granted">Allowed</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_hint_step">Installed from a file? Android may say this is a restricted setting and keep it greyed out. If so, tap the greyed-out switch once, then come back here.</string>
    <string name="setup_restricted_hint">If Android says this setting is restricted, allow restricted settings first (see the card at the top).</string>
    <string name="restricted_title">Installed from a file?</string>
    <string name="restricted_why">Android blocks usage access, notification access and accessibility for apps installed from a file, until you allow restricted settings. Skip this if you\'ve already done it.</string>
    <string name="restricted_steps">First tap Allow below on one of them and tap its greyed-out switch: Android says it\'s a restricted setting. Only then does App info offer the option: open it, tap ⋮ at the top right, then Allow restricted settings. Come back here afterwards.</string>
    <string name="restricted_open_app_info">Open App info</string>
    <string name="setup_usage_why">Needed for the dashboard and app timers: which apps you used today, and for how long.</string>
    <string name="setup_usage_not">Not used for anything else. Wellmute never sees what you do inside apps.</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_why">Counts notifications per app, and hides notifications from paused apps and from the apps you silence during Bedtime. With it, Android also gives Do Not Disturb access, so Bedtime can run as a real Android mode, with its grayscale, dimmed wallpaper, dark theme and always-on display off.</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_not">Their content is never stored or shared. Held notifications use Android\'s own snooze, so Wellmute keeps nothing of them. Wellmute doesn\'t change any other system setting.</string>
    <string name="setup_post_notifications_why">Lets Wellmute send you its own notifications:</string>
    <string name="setup_post_notifications_bedtime">Bedtime is on, and until when</string>
    <string name="setup_post_notifications_focus">Focus mode is on, and until when</string>
    <string name="setup_post_notifications_weekly">A summary of your screen time at the start of each week</string>
    <string name="setup_post_notifications_not">Only these three, and you can turn each one off in Settings → Notifications. Wellmute never sends ads or nudges to open it.</string>
    <string name="setup_optional">Optional</string>
    <string name="setup_accessibility_why">Lets Wellmute pause apps when their timer runs out or Focus mode is on, and show usage reminders if you turn them on. It only learns which app is in front.</string>
    <string name="setup_accessibility_not">It can\'t read what\'s on your screen, see what you type, or tap anything for you.</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_why">Without this, Android may stop Wellmute in the background to save battery. Timers, Focus and Bedtime would then stop working reliably, and days of history could be lost, since Android only keeps about a week of usage records.</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_not">Wellmute only wakes up for its schedules and timers; it doesn\'t run constantly.</string>
    <string name="home_pausing_off">Pausing apps is off. Your app timers and Focus mode can\'t pause anything until Wellmute is turned on again in Settings → Accessibility. This can happen if the app was force-stopped.</string>

